{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1672","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1672","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1672\",\"parent_revision\":\"58662f236e0083695d5cb0b28eec7a531cf58216\",\"root_revision\":\"3635e823fd49863f805617e67b5e7af165063cb1edab68e9798cf4a6af537940\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe `doc-drift-auditor` agent (QG T4 in `/complete-implementation`) discovers documentation drift by auditing only files that were modified in the implementation commits. This misses all files that **reference** the concepts that changed but were not themselves modified.\\n\\n**Observed in #996:** grooming swarm agent count changed from 5\u21926, required sections from 7\u21928. Auditor checked the 6 modified files but did not check `docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md`, `docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md`, `docs/backlog-lifecycle.md`, or `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/sam-pipeline.md` \u2014 none modified, all referencing stale counts. Audit passed with `status:verified`. Documentation remained stale in production.\\n\\n**Correct approach:** extract key concepts that changed from the modified files (agent names, counts, section names, dependency chains), grep the entire repo for all files referencing those concepts, audit each reference for staleness. Modified files are a **subset** of affected files, not a superset.\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: defect \u2014 scope inversion in agent SOP discovery algorithm  \\n**Pattern**: code-drift mental model applied where concept-drift model is required\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Must change:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/doc-drift-auditor.md` \u2014 SOP Step 1 (Discovery) and \\\"For Git History\\\" section\\n\\n**Review/may change:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` \u2014 `_phase_body()` for phase 4 (Option B only)\\n\\n**Tests (new test needed for AC7):**\\n- `tests/test_quality_gates.py`\\n- `tests/test_quality_gate_integration.py`\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- False assurance: `status:verified` applied to features with undetected doc drift\\n- Downstream agents receive stale counts/names as authoritative facts\\n- At minimum 4 files confirmed stale from #996 passed undetected\\n- Trust erosion in the complete-implementation quality gate\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**P1 \u2014 Quality Gate Bypass**\\n\\nT4 is a mandatory gate in `complete-implementation`. Systematic failure removes documentation correctness as a safety net. Downstream agents loading stale docs (e.g., `swarm-task-planner`, `plan-validator`) receive incorrect facts as ground truth.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] **AC1 \u2014 Concept extraction:** agent extracts named entities (agent names, counts, section names, config keys) from diffs/content of modified files before determining audit scope\\n- [ ] **AC2 \u2014 Concept grep:** for each extracted concept, agent greps entire repo for all `.md` files referencing it\\n- [ ] **AC3 \u2014 Full audit scope:** agent audits every file in the union of (modified files \u222a concept-grep results)\\n- [ ] **AC4 \u2014 #996 regression:** given the exact change in #996 (agent count 5\u21926, section count 7\u21928), the auditor includes all four previously-missed docs in its scope\\n- [ ] **AC5 \u2014 Additive scope:** modified files are still audited (concept-grep scope is additive, not replacing)\\n- [ ] **AC6 \u2014 SOP updated:** `doc-drift-auditor.md` Step 1 (Discovery) describes the concept-extraction \u2192 concept-grep \u2192 full-scope-audit algorithm\\n- [ ] **AC7 \u2014 Test/scenario:** a test or scenario document verifies the new algorithm catches the #996 pattern\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**S (Small)** \u2014 1 session, single agent\\n\\n- Agent SOP rewrite: ~1 hour\\n- `_phase_body()` update (Option B): ~30 min\\n- AC7 test/scenario: ~30 min\\n- Lint + validation: ~15 min\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. Make a change that modifies a named concept across N files (e.g., agent count 5\u21926 in 6 files, commit referencing `#996`)\\n2. Run `/complete-implementation #996`\\n3. `complete-implementation` builds T4 body with the 6 modified files as context\\n4. `doc-drift-auditor` audits those 6 files only\\n5. Four files with stale count references (`docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md`, `docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md`, `docs/backlog-lifecycle.md`, `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/sam-pipeline.md`) receive no audit\\n6. Report returns no drift findings for those files \u2192 `status:verified` applied \u2192 stale docs reach production\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on complete-implementation quality gates**, I want **doc-drift-auditor to scope its audit by changed concepts instead of only modified files** so that **documentation drift in unmodified files referencing changed concepts is reliably caught**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Quality gate gap observed during #996 implementation \u2014 user identified scope inversion\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-08\\n- **Groomed**: 2026-04-09\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-24)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n9/10 \u2014 This is a silent quality gate bypass. T4 (`doc-drift-auditor`) is a mandatory gate in `/complete-implementation`. When it passes with false negatives, `status:verified` is applied to features with undetected doc drift. Downstream agents (`swarm-task-planner`, `plan-validator`) receive stale counts and names as authoritative facts. Confirmed production failure in #996.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- **QG T4 bypass**: `doc-drift-auditor` passes silently on concept-drift that crosses unmodified files\\n- **Downstream contamination**: agents loading audited docs receive stale counts/names as ground truth\\n- **Trust erosion**: `status:verified` label no longer reliably signals documentation correctness\\n- **Confirmed blast**: at minimum 4 files from #996 (`docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md`, `docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md`, `docs/backlog-lifecycle.md`, `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/sam-pipeline.md`) reached production with stale counts after passing T4\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- T4 becomes a reliable concept-drift gate, not just a file-edit gate\\n- `status:verified` label regains its semantic guarantee\\n- Catch documentation staleness introduced by any named-concept change (counts, agent names, section names) regardless of which files were edited\\n- Eliminates the silent false-negative class that the #996 pattern represents\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen any implementation commit changes a named concept (agent name, count, section name, config key, dependency chain identifier), the auditor:\\n1. Extracts those concepts from the diff/content of modified files\\n2. Greps the entire repo for all `.md` files referencing those concepts\\n3. Audits every file in the union of (modified files \u222a concept-grep results)\\n4. Reports drift across the full scope\\n\\nModified files are always included (additive scope \u2014 concept-grep is additional, not replacing). When no concept-referencing files exist beyond the modified set, behavior is unchanged from current.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nObservable target state after the fix:\\n\\n- Running `/complete-implementation` on a change that modifies a named concept (e.g., agent count N\u2192M across K files) causes the T4 audit body to include all `.md` files that reference that concept \u2014 not only the K modified files\\n- The audit report's `## Analyzed Files` section lists both modified files AND concept-grep results explicitly, making scope visible and auditable\\n- The `doc-drift-auditor.md` SOP Step 1 (Discovery) describes the concept-extraction \u2192 concept-grep \u2192 full-scope-audit algorithm in its workflow block\\n- Given the #996 pattern (agent count 5\u21926, section count 7\u21928), the four previously-missed docs appear in the audit scope\\n- When no concept-referencing files exist beyond the modified set, behavior is unchanged from current (zero regression for simple file-only changes)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] **AC1 \u2014 Concept extraction**: agent extracts named entities (agent names, counts, section names, config keys) from diffs/content of modified files before determining audit scope\\n- [ ] **AC2 \u2014 Concept grep**: for each extracted concept, agent greps entire repo for all `.md` files referencing it\\n- [ ] **AC3 \u2014 Full audit scope**: agent audits every file in the union of (modified files \u222a concept-grep results)\\n- [ ] **AC4 \u2014 #996 regression**: given the exact change in #996 (agent count 5\u21926, section count 7\u21928), the auditor includes all four previously-missed docs (`docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md`, `docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md`, `docs/backlog-lifecycle.md`, `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/sam-pipeline.md`) in its scope\\n- [ ] **AC5 \u2014 Additive scope**: modified files are still audited (concept-grep scope is additive, not replacing)\\n- [ ] **AC6 \u2014 SOP updated**: `doc-drift-auditor.md` Step 1 (Discovery) describes the concept-extraction \u2192 concept-grep \u2192 full-scope-audit algorithm\\n- [ ] **AC7 \u2014 Coverage report**: audit report's `## Analyzed Files` section lists both modified files AND concept-grep results explicitly, so scope is visible and auditable\\n- [ ] **AC8 \u2014 Regression test**: a test or scenario document verifies the new algorithm catches the #996 pattern (concept change touches N modified files, M additional unmodified referencing files \u2014 all N+M appear in audit scope)\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Agent file | `plugins/development-harness/agents/doc-drift-auditor.md` \u2014 SOP Step 1 (Discovery) is the primary change target |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` \u2014 `_proportional_phase_body()` passes `modified_files` (Option B change) |\\n| Skill | `/dh:complete-implementation` \u2014 T4 is dispatched from this skill's QG pipeline |\\n| Test | `tests/test_quality_gates.py` \u2014 add AC7 regression scenario here |\\n| Test | `tests/test_quality_gate_integration.py` \u2014 integration coverage for scope selection |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 self-contained agent SOP change\\n- Blocks: Any feature relying on T4 as a reliable concept-drift gate (which is its stated purpose)\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 1 session, single agent\\n\\n- Agent SOP rewrite (Step 1 Discovery): ~1 hour\\n- `_phase_body()` update if Option B chosen: ~30 min\\n- AC7 regression test/scenario: ~30 min\\n- Lint and validation: ~15 min\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n**Primary \u2014 QG T4 in `/complete-implementation`:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/doc-drift-auditor.md` \u2014 SOP Step 1 (Discovery) is the direct change target; all callers of T4 are affected when this agent is dispatched\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` \u2014 `_proportional_phase_body()` passes `modified_files`; Option B extends this to also pass extracted concepts\\n\\n**Secondary \u2014 workflows that invoke T4:**\\n- `/dh:complete-implementation` skill \u2014 dispatches T4 as a mandatory quality gate; concept-based scope changes what T4 receives and checks\\n- `/dh:gate-push` skill \u2014 runs `complete-implementation` gates including T4\\n\\n**Downstream consumers of T4 output:**\\n- `status:verified` label \u2014 currently applied after a T4 pass; post-fix a pass means concept-drift was checked, not just file-edit drift\\n- Any agent loading docs marked `status:verified` (e.g., `swarm-task-planner`, `plan-validator`) \u2014 receives correct facts after fix\\n\\n**Test files:**\\n- `tests/test_quality_gates.py` \u2014 new AC8 regression scenario needed\\n- `tests/test_quality_gate_integration.py` \u2014 integration coverage for scope selection\\n\\n**No impact on:**\\n- Other quality gates (T1-T3, T5+) \u2014 scope change is isolated to T4 algorithm\\n- Backlog MCP server or SAM MCP server \u2014 no schema changes\\n- Language plugin manifests \u2014 T4 is a harness-level gate\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: defect \u2014 scope inversion in agent SOP discovery algorithm\\n**Rationale**: Agent uses `modified_files` as a proxy for `affected_files` \u2014 these sets are not equivalent when concept changes cross file boundaries. Traceable failure with specific commit history evidence from #996.\\n**Analysis Method**: 5-whys\\n**Scenario Target**: Run `/complete-implementation` after a concept rename or count change \u2192 all referencing docs appear in audit scope\\n\\n### Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n**Method**: 5-whys\\n**Classification**: defect\\n\\n#### Evidence Chain\\n\\n1. CLAIM: T4 audit passed with `status:verified` on #996 while 4 docs retained stale counts\\n   EVIDENCE: Observed production outcome \u2014 docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md et al. contained `5 agents`/`7 sections` after merge\\n   VERIFIED: yes\\n   DEPENDS ON: none (symptom)\\n\\n2. CLAIM: Auditor only checked the 6 files modified in #996 commits\\n   EVIDENCE: `doc-drift-auditor.md` SOP Step 1 \u2014 Discovery starts from `modified_files`, not a concept-grep\\n   VERIFIED: yes \u2014 agent file at `plugins/development-harness/agents/doc-drift-auditor.md` lines 61-74\\n   DEPENDS ON: 1\\n\\n3. CLAIM: Agent was designed with a file-centric scope model\\n   EVIDENCE: `quality_gates.py` `_proportional_phase_body()` passes `modified_files` list; agent receives it as audit scope\\n   VERIFIED: yes \u2014 `quality_gates.py` lines 222-268\\n   DEPENDS ON: 2\\n\\n4. CLAIM: Concept-centric scope model (\\\"what semantic entities changed\\\") was not articulated in the design\\n   EVIDENCE: No mention of concept extraction or repo-wide grep in `doc-drift-auditor.md` workflow block\\n   VERIFIED: yes \u2014 agent file lines 60-74 (entire SOP)\\n   DEPENDS ON: 3\\n\\n5. CLAIM: No test exercises scope selection behavior \u2014 defect persisted silently\\n   EVIDENCE: `test_quality_gates.py` and `test_quality_gate_integration.py` cover plan structure and dispatch, not audit scope selection\\n   VERIFIED: yes \u2014 no test asserts which files the auditor checks\\n   DEPENDS ON: 4\\n\\n**Root Cause**: `doc-drift-auditor` SOP Step 1 uses `modified_files` as the complete audit scope rather than computing `concept_grep_results \u222a modified_files`\\n**Scenario Target**: Concept change touches N files but references exist in M unmodified files \u2192 all N+M files appear in audit scope\\n\\n## Root Cause Analysis 5 Whys\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. **What?** Audit misses stale references in unmodified files\\n2. **Why?** SOP Step 1 (Discovery) inventories documentation starting from `modified_files`, not from a concept-grep across the repo\\n3. **Why?** Agent was designed with a file-centric model: \\\"what code changed\\\" \u2192 audit those files. Concept-centric model (\\\"what semantic entities changed\\\") was not articulated\\n4. **Why not caught earlier?** Tests (`test_quality_gates.py`, `test_quality_gate_integration.py`) cover SAM plan structure and dispatch, not the audit scope selection algorithm \u2014 no test exercises \\\"agent greps the right files\\\"\\n5. **Why no scope test?** Agent prompts are prose; no test framework existed for scope selection behavior. Defect persisted silently until production observation in #996\\n</div>\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Broken algorithm:**\\n```text\\n1. Receive modified_files\\n2. Audit documentation against modified_files behaviors\\n3. Report drift only for modified files\\n```\\n\\n**Correct algorithm:**\\n```text\\n1. Receive modified_files\\n2. Extract concepts from diffs/content of modified_files:\\n   - Named agents, tools, commands, section names\\n   - Counts and cardinalities (\\\"5 agents\\\", \\\"7 required sections\\\")\\n   - Dependency chain identifiers, config keys, label names\\n3. For each concept: grep -rl \\\"{concept}\\\" . (entire repo)\\n4. full_audit_scope = union(modified_files, all grep results)\\n5. Audit every file in full_audit_scope\\n6. Report drift across full scope\\n```\\n\\n**Implementation path (two options):**\\n- **Option A (agent-only):** Update `doc-drift-auditor.md` SOP Step 1. Agent derives `modified_files` from issue number via git log. No Python changes. Recommended for minimal blast radius.\\n- **Option B (explicit passing):** Update `quality_gates.py` `_phase_body()` to pass `modified_files` explicitly into T4 body. Makes scope auditable in tests.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root-Cause Analysis (5-Whys)\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. **What?** Audit misses stale references in unmodified files\\n2. **Why?** SOP Step 1 (Discovery) inventories documentation starting from `modified_files`, not from a concept-grep across the repo\\n3. **Why?** Agent was designed with a file-centric model: \\\"what code changed\\\" \u2192 audit those files. Concept-centric model (\\\"what semantic entities changed\\\") was not articulated\\n4. **Why not caught earlier?** Tests (`test_quality_gates.py`, `test_quality_gate_integration.py`) cover SAM plan structure and dispatch, not the audit scope selection algorithm \u2014 no test exercises \\\"agent greps the right files\\\"\\n5. **Why no scope test?** Agent prompts are prose; no test framework existed for scope selection behavior. Defect persisted silently until production observation in #996\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"834be35ab1d43bdf3a82801d89251a9028b04e506a2f51d223986abc939f7040\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg4sfQ\"}"}